A||||23||Shiner||Engraved Plenum: what up with that?||||5||
Z||000000||Shiner||03-01-2000||12:49 AM||||The intake plenum on my '87 GT has the "FIERO" letters actually sunken into the metal.  Most (I think all) of the other fiero V6's I have seen have a sticker there instead.  What is the deal with this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||03-01-2000||01:32 AM||||Am I right in assuming the plenums are interchangable between the V6 models?<P>I'm pretty sure they are, as the engine is the same. I was thinking it'd be cool to get a plenum without Fiero engraved in it, and then get something else engraved.. a simple line art pegasus would be cool.. or even just GM 2.8, or something similar to the 3.4L||||reg||1
Z||000002||Uaana||03-01-2000||02:33 AM||||Must just be an 87 thing.. My GT has the same<BR>intake.  <BR>IMHO I like it.. Not ashamed of my girls heritage.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||03-01-2000||03:23 AM||||85 and 86 were stickers 87 and 88 were engraved.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||03-01-2000||06:32 AM||||I'm pretty sure that all of the 2.8 plenums were identical other than the engraving.  Good idea, Darklord.  I think I'll do that.  <P>Darklord--Any progress on the server thing?||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||03-01-2000||08:05 AM||||Monkeyman, do you still have the pic of my engine? It is kinda hard to make out, but I put a V6-H.O. badge from the front fender of a 99 GrandAm on my plenum. Cost $7 at the dealership and looks very clean in "real life". <BR>BTW I have an extra "non-engraved" plenum for sale cheap if anyone is interested||||reg||1
