Z||000011||stimpy||03-01-2000||07:34 PM||||Darklord, real easy. The badge is self adhesive. Just peel and stick. You would want to clean the area well before applying it, but once it is on, stays just fine. If you think that looks cool, my dad put GTP-supercharged badges on his red 86 GT 3.8 s/c. You can get all kinds of goodies from mr. Goodwrench parts dept.!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Phaeton||03-02-2000||12:22 AM||||Golly, I thought all V6 Fieros had "FIERO" cast into the plenum cover.  I need to get out and get under more hoods.||||reg||1
Z||000013||JetroGT||03-02-2000||04:45 AM||||Insted of acutally ingraving the intake you could use a scroll saw to cut the fiero letters into a thin piece of stainless sheet metal. Then glue it on  over the center of the intake with epoxy. ||||reg||3
Z||000014||Monkeyman||03-02-2000||07:13 AM||||I was thinking about something other than "FIERO".||||reg||1
Z||000015||Uaana||03-04-2000||08:10 AM||||Hey monkey<BR>Have you thougt about going to the Accel wires? They would go great with the rest of<BR>the yellow on your intake and covers.||||reg||1
Z||000016||stimpy||03-04-2000||08:42 AM||||Ummm, Monkey, o.k. if I field this one? <BR>Actually that is a pic of my engine that Monkey posted for me as I am technologically challenged (WebTv).<BR>Those actually are Accel 8mm Super Stock spiral core wires.  I looked for the yellow Accel wires and when I found them I noticed that they are only 7mm, have a very porous feeling jacket, and look kinda cheap. Accel doesn't make the 8mm in yellow, at least they dn have it at the auto parts store I patronize.<BR>The wires I have are much smoother, so the are much easier to clean and have a nice glossy shine. I think the red sets a nice contrast. <BR>Also I have heard that the cheaper Accel wires put on a groovy light show at night...lots of arcing.||||reg||1
Z||000017||batboy||03-04-2000||09:42 AM||||I've used Accel for years, even back when their cheap stuff was good. Unfortunately nowadays, you have to buy Accel's top of the line to get the good quality stuff. Those 8mm spiral core wires are excellent. Right now, I'm looking in my JEGS catalog and you can get a universal V8 kit in the 8mm spiral core wires in both blue and yellow for $45. It's a simple matter of cutting the wires to fit your V6, plus you'll have a couple extra wires to use as spares.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Uaana||03-05-2000||02:20 AM||||Just in case you are still looking for good<BR>yellow wires I just got my 8.8mm spiral core<BR>Accels from Summit for 43.99 + 6.00 shipping<BR>and they are custom fit. No cutting <BR>Very nice and glossy I am quite happy with them as they have helped get rid of that constant throttle surge. (msd coil next payday to finish that)<BR>And yes the old wires were shot 8mm's||||reg||1
Z||000019||GWMORGAN||03-05-2000||11:49 AM||||What's the part# on those Accel 8.8mm plug wires, also can they be fitted with the plug wire heat jacket that come on the fiero?<BR>Thanks for info.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000020||Uaana||03-05-2000||10:48 PM||||Oops sorry about that<BR>the part number is Accel 8879 <BR>And yes they do fit in the factory heat shields.<BR>And that was at Summit Racing <BR>1-800-230-3030 Order line<BR>1-800-517-1035 Customer Service<BR>And no I do not work for them just trying to help out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000021||bHooper||03-06-2000||08:38 PM||||as for the "earliest" engraved plenum's... my '86.5 GT is engraved!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>does that make me special?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000022||Patrick's Dad||03-06-2000||09:30 PM||||Cool badge on the plenum. My 88 Formula, as you may guess, is engraved, which doesn't bother me at all. I'd worry more that the adhesive would melt, or otherwise fail to stick as the bay heats up.<P>As for me, when I finish the bodywork, I plan to get the "Formula" script badges from the Firebird and place them on the rear quarters above and behind the rear wheel. I may also place one on the L headlamp cover, although the "Pontiac" is inset on the other....||||reg||1
Z||000023||stimpy||03-06-2000||10:44 PM||||The melting adhesive thing was a concern for me too. I didn't know for sure if it would work, but the cheesy little Fiero decal didn't have any problem, so I figured it would be safe. Plus I figured that these were designed to go on the fenders. Ever touch a black car in hot sun? I don't think my plenum ever gets THAT hot (ouch!). Not to mention the abuse from carwashes, etc.  So far it has held up well.<BR>Even more of a concern was that the plastic that the badge is made of would warp. Again- so far, so good.||||reg||1
